<title>FRANCE: French treasury head says EMU delay unimaginable.</title>
<headline>French treasury head says EMU delay unimaginable.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French treasury director Jean Lemierre said on Wednesday it was &quot;unimaginable&quot; that European monetary union would not be launched as planned in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not believe that where we are now, in December 1996, given what has been said and what has been done, the single currency will not be launched,&quot; he told a business conference.</p>
<p>He had been asked whether there was any risk of a delay to monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;It seems unimaginable to me,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
